To ensure security, you should use the `htmlspecialchars()` function to escape special characters in the output. This function converts special characters to their HTML entities, which prevents XSS attacks. Here's an example of how to use it:

```php
function safe_html_output($data) {
    return htmlspecialchars($data, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8');
}

// Usage
echo safe_html_output("<script>alert('XSS');</script>");
```

This approach ensures that any special characters in the input are safely escaped, preventing any potential XSS attacks.
